 The problem is a transient heat conduction problem with convection at the surface. The Biot number is Bi = hL/k = 2*(1/12)/25 = 0.00333, which is very small, so we can use the lumped capacitance method. The temperature change is given by θ = θ_i e^{-hA/V ρ Cp}, where A is the surface area, V is the volume, and θ_i is the initial temperature difference. A = 4πr² = 4π(1/12)², V = (4/3)πr³ = (4/3)π(1/12)³. So A/V = 3/r = 36. Then θ = 520 e^{-2*36} = 520 e^{-72} ≈ 0.
