d = 1 mm = 1 x 10^-3 m

First, calculate the difference in refractive indices:
n_R - n_L = 1.55610 - 1.55821 = -0.00211

Now, calculate the rotation angle in radians:
θ = (2π / 396.0 x 10^-9) * (-0.00211) * (1 x 10^-3)

θ = (2 * 3.14159 / 396.0 x 10^-9) * (-0.00211) * (1 x 10^-3)

θ = (6.28318 / 396.0 x 10^-9) * (-0.00211) * (1 x 10^-3)

θ = 1.5866 x 10^6 * (-0.00211) * (1 x 10^-3)

θ = -3.343 x 10^-3 radians

